      "train_qid": "28054",
      "hint": "For puzzles where agents announce ignorance, first write down exactly what each agent knows. If the setup leaves ambiguous which of two quantities was revealed, that ambiguity is part of every agent's uncertainty: do not case-split externally, assume one reading, and restart. An agent holding x who sees N must keep every partner value legal under either reading (sum/product reveal: N-x and N/x when each is a valid natural number). \"I do not know\" means at least two partner values survive, which constrains that agent's own number. Apply announcements in order, filtering the set left by the previous one. Verify at the end: your candidate makes both announcements true and no rival candidate does. Track eliminations once and move forward instead of relitigating; looping exhausts your budget before you answer.",
